  + [status] is strong_kernel_architecture_candidate_SJS_required

& [CoreConclusion] is supported as the first semantic governance layer
  + Observer then Honesty then Security with Observer closure should precede every non-kernel SOP pattern, provider, model-directed program, tool, recovered state, and effect capability
  + this OHS confirmation kernel gives the identity-recognition layer its startup governor and makes the later faculty cycle conditional on a proved boot identity
  + lower deterministic primitives must still measure, verify, compare, preserve, and halt; they are trusted computing-base mechanisms rather than separately loaded semantic patterns
  + self-recognition cannot be proved by faculty agreement alone and requires a bootstrap identity contract plus measurement anchored outside the state being judged
  = concise: measure first, let OHS judge the measurement, seal one boot identity, and only then admit patterns

& [KernelLayering] prevents semantic and physical kernel conflation
  + [layer_minus_one] is host, hardware, operating-system, secure-boot, TPM, external verifier, or operator trust root when available
  + [layer_zero_primitives] are bounded read, measure, digest, signature verify, exact compare, append record, zeroize, and halt operations
  + [layer_one_OHS_kernel] is the first semantic pattern and contains only startup identity formation, independent confirmation, disposition, and proof emission
  + [layer_two_recognition_runtime] admits the exact signed package set and immutable runtime generation authorized by the confirmed identity
  + [layer_three_patterns] contains query microkernel, remaining faculties, Cantor programs, model providers, tools, reentry, and effect proposals
  - never: claim layer-one semantics replace host isolation, executable integrity, memory protection, or hardware roots
  - never: load layer-three material to decide whether layer-three material was safe to load

& [StartupIdentityContract] declares the expected self before runtime admission
  + [contract_id] is immutable, signed, versioned, and externally pinned
  + [kernel_binary_digest] binds the exact OHS implementation or bytecode interpreter and program
  + [compiler_and_profile] bind the admitted compiler, protocol, schema, and kernel version
  + [trust_root_set] binds signer identities, public keys, roles, revocation inputs, and delegation limits
  + [configuration_digest] binds all startup configuration that can change behavior
  + [expected_runtime_generation] binds environment profile, ordered package set, dependency lock, trust time policy, and semantic fabric root
  + [purpose_and_authority] bind principal, startup purpose, capability ceiling, effect boundary, and expiry
  + [persistent_state_policy] defines whether startup is clean, recovered, or reentered and names every admitted state root
  + [environment_requirements] bind platform, isolation, resource, channel, path, and threat-model assumptions material to identity
  + [failure_policy] binds fail-closed, diagnostic, recovery, zeroization, and restart behavior
  - never: let the runtime under examination replace or broaden its own expected identity contract

& [StartupMeasurement] is independently acquired actual state
  + [measurement_id] is fresh and nonce-bound
  + [measurer_identity] states the root or supervisor that acquired the facts
  + [measured_binary_digest] and [measured_configuration_digest] cover actual loaded bytes and behavior-affecting configuration
  + [measured_trust_roots] preserve actual keys, policy, revocation, and dependency-lock state
  + [measured_runtime_inputs] preserve exact package, environment, persistent-state, authority, purpose, and effect inputs proposed for admission
  + [environment_evidence] preserves isolation and channel facts that can actually be observed
  + [unmeasured_surface] explicitly identifies memory, firmware, hardware, provider, process, path, time, or external-state regions outside evidence
  + [measurement_proof] binds acquisition lineage and exact bytes
  - never: let a self-reported digest substitute for an independently obtained measurement

& [OperationalUncontaminated] is bounded and falsifiable
  + every behavior-affecting startup input is either measured and admitted or identified as unavailable and materiality-judged
  + no model output, tool result, network message, prior mutable cache, unrecognized persisted state, or non-kernel SOP pattern influenced the confirmation
  + measured identity equals the pinned StartupIdentityContract on every constitutive field
  + no active boundary signal, stale trust input, revoked package, unexpected authority, open effect channel, or unaccounted state root remains
  + the claim is scoped to the declared measurement boundary, threat model, time, and evidence
  = valid_result: no detected material contamination or breach within the attested scope
  - never: claim metaphysical purity, inaccessible-history certainty, or global absence of compromise

& [ObserverOpening] forms the candidate self-identity frame
  + read only the pinned StartupIdentityContract and independently acquired StartupMeasurement
  + name subject, purpose, expected identity, actual measurement, scope, unavailable surfaces, and materiality policy
  + emit one candidate StartupIdentityFrame without admitting it
  + require exact separate Honesty and Security activation identities
  - never: predeclare confirmation or suppress a mismatch to continue startup

& [HonestyConfirmation] tests correspondence and authentic self-description
  + compare every claimed self-identity field with measured evidence and source lineage
  + detect identity substitution, stale or omitted component, false continuity, assumption laundering, unknown measurement, and unsupported no-breach claim
  + distinguish exact, qualified, contradicted, unavailable, and unresolved results
  + emit a signed or digest-bound independent return whose failure cannot be waived by Security
  - never: infer correctness from successful signature verification alone

& [SecurityConfirmation] tests integrity, isolation, authority, and closed effects
  + independently recheck trust roots, package lifecycle, dependency lock, revocation, configuration, path, process boundary, persisted state, authority ceiling, and effect channels
  + evaluate the Honesty return without treating it as a substitute for Security evidence
  + detect unmeasured mutable influence, sandbox escape, ambient authority, recovery-state injection, rollback, confused deputy, and premature capability activation
  + emit a separate return whose failure cannot be waived by Honesty
  - never: open listeners, model providers, general tools, network, recovered sessions, or effects before final Observer confirmation

& [ObserverClosure] seals or rejects one startup identity
  + [confirmed] requires exact or explicitly allowed qualified Honesty and Security returns, no material unresolved surface, and matching contract and measurement roots
  + [recovery_only] permits only a separately pinned minimal recovery surface with normal patterns, effects, and trust inheritance disabled
  + [blocked] produces bounded diagnostic proof and halts admission
  + [unresolved] holds startup when required evidence cannot be acquired safely
  + the closure emits one immutable KernelIdentityAttestation and one exact startup disposition
  + any input mutation after measurement invalidates the attestation and restarts the loop with a new generation
  - never: use majority vote, model confidence, repeated agreement, or elapsed time as confirmation

& [KernelIdentityAttestation] is the only semantic admission token
  + [attestation_id] is content-addressed
  + [contract_ref] and [measurement_ref] bind expected and actual identity
  + [observer_opening_ref], [honesty_return_ref], [security_return_ref], and [observer_closure_ref] bind the complete OHS round
  + [runtime_generation_digest] binds the exact generation permitted to activate
  + [allowed_pattern_roots] bind the exact query microkernel and further pattern package roots that may load
  + [authority_ceiling] and [effect_boundary] remain no broader than startup policy
  + [issued_at], [expires_at], [nonce], and [invalidation_predicates] prevent replay and stale reuse
  + [residual_uncertainty] remains visible to every later frame
  - never: let an attestation authorize a different runtime generation, package root, principal, purpose, pattern set, or effect boundary

& [BoundedConfirmationLoop] is Observer to Honesty to Security to Observer
  * acquire contract and measurement through layer-zero primitives
  * Observer emits candidate StartupIdentityFrame
  * Honesty emits correspondence return
  * Security emits integrity and admissibility return
  * Observer emits confirmed, recovery_only, blocked, or unresolved disposition
  * layer zero records attestation or fault and activates nothing else on failure
  + one changed input creates a new round identity rather than mutating a prior round
  + repeated rounds are bounded and require new evidence rather than rhetorical reconsideration
  + successful closure seals the exact generation before layer-three loading begins

& [StartupModes] are closed
  + [cold_clean] admits no prior semantic state except pinned bootstrap authority
  + [governed_reentry] admits only exact signed reentry roots under an explicit persistent-state policy
  + [reconstituted_boundary] admits only a new boundary and trust state already proved under a separate recovery authority
  + [recovery_only] exposes minimal diagnostic and repair operations from a separately pinned recovery root
  + [blocked] and [unresolved] activate no normal runtime
  - never: reinterpret degraded or accommodated prior state as a clean boot

& [BreachResponse] integrates the prior reconstitution model
  + a detected startup breach cannot be accommodated inside the normal runtime it was meant to authorize
  + normal package and pattern loading remains blocked
  + recovery occurs through a separately rooted minimal environment whose authority cannot inherit from the breached generation
  + successful recovery produces a new StartupIdentityContract, ReconstitutedIdentityBoundary, stability standard, measurement, and generation
  + the OHS kernel reruns from the new roots before normal activation
  + predecessor breach and revocation lineage remain inspectable

& [PrimalScribeRefinerReconciliation] preserves lower obligations without loading other faculties
  + layer-zero append-only recording fulfills the primal inscription obligation needed to preserve measurement and attestation
  + exact comparison and smallest fail-closed disposition fulfill bounded refinement obligations at startup
  + this does not load the composed Scribe or Refiner faculty patterns before OHS confirmation
  + after confirmation the full integrated faculty cycle retains all seven faculties and their independent duties

& [CurrentImplementationFit] is partial and favorable
  + current trust admission, recognition certificates, environment digest, PreparedRuntime generation identity, whole-generation activation, pinned service configuration, and fail-closed startup provide implementation substrate
  + current query microkernel is a minimal signed bootstrap primer but is not preceded by a formal OHS semantic confirmation round
  + current FacultyCycle requires Honesty and Security boundaries but does not define a bootstrap-only OHS profile or KernelIdentityAttestation
  + current resident service verifies configuration, environment, packages, fabric, and PreparedRuntime before listening, but does not claim independent self-measurement or uncontaminated process identity
  + no current implementation proves hardware, executable-memory, firmware, operating-system, or external measurement roots

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is OHSK-001 through OHSK-018
  + [OHSK-001] define OHS as the first semantic pattern and forbid all layer-three loading before closure
  + [OHSK-002] define layer-minus-one roots, layer-zero primitives, layer-one OHS, layer-two recognition runtime, and layer-three patterns
  + [OHSK-003] define immutable externally pinned StartupIdentityContract
  + [OHSK-004] define independently acquired nonce-bound StartupMeasurement and explicit unmeasured surface
  + [OHSK-005] define operational uncontaminated and no-detected-breach claims under exact scope and threat model
  + [OHSK-006] define Observer opening, Honesty confirmation, Security confirmation, and Observer closure as separate records
  + [OHSK-007] prohibit one faculty from waiving the other's material failure
  + [OHSK-008] define immutable KernelIdentityAttestation bound to exact generation, pattern roots, authority, effects, time, nonce, and residual uncertainty
  + [OHSK-009] invalidate and restart on any post-measurement identity input change
  + [OHSK-010] define cold_clean, governed_reentry, reconstituted_boundary, recovery_only, blocked, and unresolved startup modes
  + [OHSK-011] permit no normal pattern, provider, tool, listener, recovered session, or effect activation before confirmation
  + [OHSK-012] root recovery separately and prohibit breached-generation trust inheritance
  + [OHSK-013] preserve primal inscription and bounded comparison as deterministic primitives without loading composed Scribe or Refiner patterns
  + [OHSK-014] distinguish artifact identity, semantic correspondence, operational integrity, and inaccessible compromise
  + [OHSK-015] make every claim about contamination and breach falsifiable by declared measurement and unavailable surfaces
  + [OHSK-016] test valid cold boot, valid reentry, signed false identity, stale measurement, revoked root, configuration drift, package substitution, recovered-state injection, open effect channel, unavailable evidence, recovery, and replay
  + [OHSK-017] compare software-only external pinning, supervisor measurement, operating-system signing, TPM or secure-boot attestation, and offline verifier profiles without claiming unavailable guarantees
  + [OHSK-018] preserve exact boot proof and identity lineage for later faculty rechecks and query results

& [Decision] is reorder the candidate architecture around OHS startup confirmation
  + [canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [execution_authority] is absent
  + [signed_package_change] is none
  + [schedule_effect] OHSK-SJS-01 becomes a prerequisite to general HSIBI transition integration and any claim that the query microkernel is the first semantic startup pattern
  + [next] audit current bootstrap, trust, PreparedRuntime, service, faculty, reentry, recovery, effect, and platform-measurement authorities before choosing the smallest truthful root profile
